### What I found when triaging
Juice Shop is intentionally vulnerable, so many findings in `routes/`,
`server.ts` and `data/static/codefixes/` are likely deliberate challenge
code rather than bugs to fix.

The 18 pipeline findings split into two groups. Five are in
`security-scan.yml`, which I wrote, so those are mine to fix. The rest are
in workflow files that appear to come from upstream Juice Shop. The 18 pipeline 
findings split into two groups. Five are in `security-scan.yml`, which I wrote, 
so those are mine to fix. The rest are in workflow files that appear to come 
from upstream Juice Shop.

All five of mine are the same rule, `github-actions-mutable-action-tag`
(lines 17, 32, 52, 64 and 76). Each step references an action by a tag
such as `@v3`, and a tag can be repointed by the action's owner, so a
compromised action could run malicious code in my pipeline. I plan to pin
each one to a full commit SHA and re-run the scan to confirm the findings
clear.

### Limitations
This is a learning project and a small script. It only reads Semgrep's
JSON format, it doesn't deduplicate findings, and it doesn't read the
ZAP results yet